  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-09T03:05:39.036Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While some people may enjoy sorting images into folders, this may not be ideal for others. Personally, I've always found this to be very annoying as it makes searching for specific images vastly more tedious. When there are hundreds of folders, each with dozens or hundreds of images, it makes scrolling though them to find specific images challenging. I also have this folder used by Adobe Bridge & Lightroom to further edit images as I capture them. Having additional folders makes this slightly more annoying. Many computers use SSDs and are plenty powerful enough to open folders with many thousands of images and despite amassing well over 10K images, I've not experienced lag personally managing these.\n\nAn example of how this could wind up being fairly annoying. I've played almost daily since 2018. Those 10K images would be sorted into over 1,000 folders. Talk about tedious to look through.\n\nWhile adding another menu option to change this may not be ideal, it would however be nice if there was a launch option that could be set where the option of folder saving could be disabled for those who dislike that. If this is already possible, I didn't notice it in the notes.",
